<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valsad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bulsar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valsad, formerly Bulsar, is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the headquarters of Valsad district. The district covers the coastal plain and the forested hills of the former princely state of Dharampur. The area is well known for its mangoes, especially the Alphonso variety.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valsad.jpg" alt="Valsad" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bhartiya97 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valsad_City_View_from_Parnera_Hill_in_Gujarat,India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
